WEBVTT

00:06:59.673 --> 00:07:02.379
And yet it can point
to a tiny region of sky.

00:07:02.403 --> 00:07:06.705
For 11 and a half days,
it did it in sections,

00:07:06.729 --> 00:07:09.383
accurately enough
to take amazing images like this.

00:07:09.407 --> 00:07:10.566
So the question is:

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:13.004
How does something
that is not touching anything

00:07:13.028 --> 00:07:14.189
know where it is?

00:07:14.213 --> 00:07:17.174
The answer is that right in the middle
of it, it has something

00:07:17.198 --> 00:07:19.569
that, to my great disappointment,
isn't a raw egg,

00:07:19.593 --> 00:07:21.132
but basically does the same job.

00:07:21.156 --> 00:07:23.035
It's got gyroscopes which are spinning,

00:07:23.059 --> 00:07:25.863
and because of the law
of conservation of angular momentum,

00:07:25.887 --> 00:07:28.461
they keep spinning
with the same axis, indefinitely.

00:07:28.485 --> 00:07:31.574
Hubble kind of rotates around them,
and so it can orient itself.